86492806 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "ea73b3dd-bf88-5f7b-9b97-f1ed24555540" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492847 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186492765 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492847 #edb/ref 1069 "q-143978" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492847 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492847 #edb/ref 1071 "In a hardware store, there are three boxes containing light bulbs. Box $A$ contains $15$ bulbs, of which $2$ are defective, and box $B$ contains $10$ bulbs, of which $1$ is defective. A box is selected at random, and a bulb is randomly chosen from the box. If the probability that the selected bulb is defective is $\\frac{2}{15},$ what is the probability that a randomly selected bulb from box $C$ is defective?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492847 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "33d92120-f62e-56e8-8525-dfbf23370577" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492847 #edb/ref 1074 "Let $D$ be the event of selecting a defective bulb at random from one of the three boxes, and   \n\n- let $A$ be the event that the bulb is from box $A,$\n\n- let $B$ be the event that the bulb is  from box $B$\n\n- let $C$ be the event that the bulb is from box $C.$\n\nThen the disjoint union $A⊔B⊔C$ covers the entire sample space. \n\nTo calculate the probability of selecting a defective bulb, we can use the law of total probability: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(D) & =P(D\\cap A)+P(D\\cap B)+P(D\\cap C) \\\\  & =P(D|A)P(A)+P(D|B)P(B)+P(D|C)P(C)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's go through the problem statement and translate each piece of information into mathematical notation. \n\n- Since a box is chosen at random, we have\n\n$$\nP(A)=P(B)=P(C)=\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$\n\n- Since there are $2$ defective bulbs out of $15$  in box $A$ and  $1$ defective bulb out of $10$ in box $B,$  we have \n\n$$\nP(D|A)=\\frac{2}{15},\\,P(D|B)=\\frac{1}{10}.\n$$\n\n- Since the probability that a randomly selected bulb is defective is $\\frac{2}{15},$ we have\n\n$$\nP(D)=\\frac{2}{15}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above information into the law of total probability and solving for $P(D|C),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(D) & =P(D|A)P(A)+P(D|B)P(B)+P(D|C)P(C) \\\\ \\frac{2}{15} & =(\\frac{2}{15})(\\frac{1}{3})+(\\frac{1}{10})(\\frac{1}{3})+P(D|C)(\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\ \\frac{2}{15} & =\\frac{2}{45}+\\frac{1}{30}+\\frac{1}{3}P(D|C) \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}P(D|C) & =\\frac{1}{18} \\\\ P(D|C) & =\\frac{1}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the probability that a randomly selected bulb from box $C$ is defective is $\\frac{1}{6}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492892 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186492707 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492892 #edb/ref 1069 "q-143721" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492892 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492892 #edb/ref 1071 "Three factories produce the same tool for the market. Factory $A$ produces $30%$ of the tools, of which $2%$ are defective. Factory $B$ produces $34%$ of the tools, of which $5%$ are defective, and factory $C$ produces $36%$ of the tools, of which $5%$ are defective. What is the probability that a randomly selected tool is defective?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492892 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a98874b4-d2c1-50c9-83d1-a1b2a1981db4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492892 #edb/ref 1074 "Let $D$ be the event that a randomly selected tool is defective, and \n\n- let $A$ be the event that the tool was produced by factory $A,$\n\n- let $B$ be the event that the tool was produced by factory $B,$\n\n- let $C$ be the event that the tool was produced by factory $C.$\n\nThen the disjoint union $A⊔B⊔C$ covers the entire sample space.\n\nTo calculate the probability that a randomly selected tool is defective, we can use the law of total probability:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(D) & =P(D\\cap A)+P(D\\cap B)+P(D\\cap C) \\\\  & =P(D|A)P(A)+P(D|B)P(B)+P(D|C)P(C)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's go through the problem statement and translate each piece of information into mathematical notation.\n\n- Since factory $A$ produces $30%$ of the tools, factory $B$ produces $34%$ of the tools, and factory $C$ produces $36%$ of the tools, we have\n\n$$\nP(A)=0.3,\\,P(B)=0.34,\\,P(C)=0.36.\n$$\n\n- Since $2%$ of the tools produced by factory $A$, $5%$ of the tools produced by factory $B$, and $5%$ of the tools produced by factory $C,$ are defective, we have \n\n$$\nP(D|A)=0.02,\\,P(D|B)=0.05,\\,P(D|C)=0.05.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above information into the law of total probability, the probability that a randomly selected tool is defective is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(D) & =P(D|A)P(A)+P(D|B)P(B)+P(D|C)P(C) \\\\  & =(0.02)(0.3)+(0.05)(0.34)+(0.05)(0.36) \\\\  & =0.006+0.017+0.018 \\\\  & =0.041.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492894 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186492802 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492894 #edb/ref 1069 "q-143759" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492894 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492894 #edb/ref 1071 "Ann has three email accounts. In the first account, she receives $40%$ of her emails, of which $10%$ are spam. In the second account, she receives $35%$ of her emails, of which $8%$ are spam. And in the third account, she receives $25%$ of her emails, of which $8%$ are spam. Based on this data, what is the probability that a randomly selected email from any of Ann's accounts is spam?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492894 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "aa34c10c-c85d-5965-879f-040a2dcc2a58" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492894 #edb/ref 1074 "Let $S$ be the event that the selected email is spam, and\n\n- let ${A}_{1}$ be the event that the email was received in the first account,\n\n- let ${A}_{2}$ be the event that the email was received in the second account,\n\n- let ${A}_{3}$ be the event that the email was received in the third account.\n\nThen the disjoint union ${A}_{1}⊔{A}_{2}⊔{A}_{3}$ covers the entire sample space.\n\nTo calculate the probability that a randomly selected email is spam, we use the law of total probability:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(S) & =P(S\\cap {A}_{1})+P(S\\cap {A}_{2})+P(S\\cap {A}_{3}) \\\\  & =P(S|{A}_{1})P({A}_{1})+P(S|{A}_{2})P({A}_{2})+P(S|{A}_{3})P({A}_{3})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's go through the problem statement and translate each piece of information into mathematical notation.\n\n- Since Ann receives $40%$ of her emails in the first account,  $35%$ in the second account, and $25%$ in the third account, we have\n\n$$\nP({A}_{1})=0.4,\\,P({A}_{2})=0.35,\\,P({A}_{3})=0.25.\n$$\n\n- Since $10%$ of the emails received in the first account, $8%$ of the emails received in the first account, and $8%$ of the emails received in the third account are spam, we have\n\n$$\nP(S|{A}_{1})=0.1,\\,P(S|{A}_{2})=0.08\\,P(S|{A}_{3})=0.08.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above information into the law of total probability, the probability that a randomly selected email from any of Ann's accounts is spam is   \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(S) & =P(S|{A}_{1})P({A}_{1})+P(S|{A}_{2})P({A}_{2})+P(S|{A}_{3})P({A}_{3}) \\\\  & =(0.1)(0.4)+(0.08)(0.35)+(0.08)(0.25) \\\\  & =0.04+0.028+0.02 \\\\  & =0.088.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492917 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186492806 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492917 #edb/ref 1069 "q-143559" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492917 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492917 #edb/ref 1071 "A company manufactures electronic components. The components are produced by three machines, $A,$ $B,$ and $C.$ In a particular random sample, $31$ of the components were produced by machine $A,$ $34$ by machine $B,$ and $35$ by machine $C.$ On inspecting the sample for defective components, it was found that $2$ defective components were produced by machine $A,$ $1$  by machine $B,$ and $2$  by machine $C.$ Based on this data, what is the probability that a randomly selected component from the sample is defective?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492917 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e343068f-45c7-52dd-ac5c-c29d4a7a5cbc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492917 #edb/ref 1074 "Let $S$ be the event that the chosen component is defective, and \n\n- let $A$ be the event that the  component was produced  by  machine $A,$\n\n- let $B$ be the event that the  component was produced  by  machine $B,$\n\n- let $C$ be the event that the  component was produced  by  machine $C.$\n\nThen the disjoint union $A⊔B⊔C$ covers the entire sample space.\n\nTo calculate the probability that a randomly selected component from the sample is defective, we use the law of total probability:  \n\n$$\nP(S)=P(S\\cap A)+P(S\\cap B)+P(S\\cap C)\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that there is a total of \n\n$$\n31+34+35=100\n$$\n\ncomponents in the sample.\n\n- To calculate $P(S\\cap A),$ we take the number defective components produced by machine $A$ $(2)$ and divide by the total number of components produced $(100).$ So, we have\n\n$$\nP(S\\cap A)=\\frac{2}{100}.\n$$\n\n- To calculate $P(S\\cap B),$ we take the number defective components produced by machine $B$ $(1)$ and divide by the total number of components produced  $(100).$ So, we have \n\n$$\nP(S\\cap B)=\\frac{1}{100}.\n$$\n\n- To calculate $P(S\\cap C),$ we take the number defective components produced by machine $C$ $(2)$ and divide by the total number of components produced  $(100).$ So, we have \n\n$$\nP(S\\cap C)=\\frac{2}{100}.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the above information into the law of total probability, the probability that a randomly component is defective is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(S) & =P(S\\cap A)+P(S\\cap B)+P(S\\cap C) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{100}+\\frac{1}{100}+\\frac{2}{100} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{100} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{20}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492947 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186492977 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492947 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "48161813-f84d-504c-b8c4-db0136c2de37" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492947 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186492917 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492953 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186492947 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492953 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "64fd50f2-7184-51d1-b27f-040fb0e0ea7c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492953 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186092559 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492970 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186492981 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492970 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "90883805-26ab-5fc5-bb58-296a7633b093" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492970 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186492894 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492977 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186492970 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492977 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a2414de0-21e9-54d6-9573-da1fa9464bbd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492977 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186492892 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492981 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a66ad3c1-21d4-525d-b81a-6c389b90b1cb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492981 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186492847 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
